  "verbalization": "Flurbiprofen is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c9 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Flurbiprofen causes Bleeding Tendency, which is mediated by Montelukast, and that Montelukast binds to Cyp2c9. Similarly, Flurbiprofen causes Oesophageal Disorder, which is linked to Omeprazole, and Omeprazole also binds to Cyp2c9. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Flurbiprofen influences Cyp2c9 through the interaction of its metabolites with the enzyme. The lowest common ancestor of these relationships is the class of compounds shared by Flurbiprofen and its metabolites, suggesting a broader functional role in modulating Cyp2c9 activity. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Cyp2c9 in the metabolic response to Flurbiprofen, particularly through the binding of its metabolites.",
